<title>SINGAPORE: TABLE-Pacific Can 1st half loss narrows.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Pacific Can 1st half loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				 5.40  vs   6.16</p>
<p>    Loss per share (cts)		 7.30  vs   8.80</p>
<p>    Loss per shr fully diluted (cts) 5.30  vs   6.40</p>
<p>    Turnover				25.84  vs  25.02</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.50  vs   0.43</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   0.46  vs   0.39</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	  2.16  vs   2.05</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			   5.19  vs   6.34</p>
<p>    Loss from associates		 0.09  vs   0.07 (gain)</p>
<p>    Tax					0.34  vs   0.14</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (gain)) 0.22  vs   0.24</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	    (loss)  0.49  vs   0.78 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - Pacific Can Investment Holdings Ltd said its extraordinary items related to the closure of a sales unit in China and its share of costs involved with an associated company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
